      <h1 id="installing-openstack-network-config" class="group scroll-mt-20">Configuring network settings after installing OpenStack<a href="#installing-openstack-network-config" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p class="_abstract">You can configure network settings for an OpenShift Container Platform on Red Hat OpenStack Platform (RHOSP) cluster after installation.</p>
      <h2 id="installation-osp-configuring-api-floating-ip_installing-openstack-network-config" class="group scroll-mt-20">Configuring application access with floating IP addresses<a href="#installation-osp-configuring-api-floating-ip_installing-openstack-network-config" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">After you install OpenShift Container Platform, configure Red Hat OpenStack Platform (RHOSP) to allow application network traffic by attaching a floating IP address to the ingress port.</p>
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>You do not need to perform this procedure if you provided values for <code>platform.openstack.apiFloatingIP</code> and <code>platform.openstack.ingressFloatingIP</code> in the <code>install-config.yaml</code> file, or <code>os_api_fip</code> and <code>os_ingress_fip</code> in the <code>inventory.yaml</code> playbook, during installation. The floating IP addresses are already set.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>OpenShift Container Platform cluster must be installed</li>
      <li>Floating IP addresses are enabled as described in the OpenShift Container Platform on RHOSP installation documentation.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Attach a floating IP address to the ingress port by completing the following commands:
      <ol>
      <li>
      Show the port by entering the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ openstack port show <cluster_name>-<cluster_ID>-ingress-port"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Attach the port to the IP address by entering the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ openstack floating ip set --port <ingress_port_ID> <apps_FIP>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      </li>
      <li>
      Add a wildcard <code>A</code> record for <code>*apps.</code> to your DNS file:
      <CodeBlock code={"*.apps.<cluster_name>.<base_domain>  IN  A  <apps_FIP>"} lang="dns" />
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>If you do not control the DNS server but want to enable application access for non-production purposes, you can add these hostnames to the <code>/etc/hosts</code> file:</p>
          <CodeBlock code={"<apps_FIP> console-openshift-console.apps.<cluster name>.<base domain>\n<apps_FIP> integrated-oauth-server-openshift-authentication.apps.<cluster name>.<base domain>\n<apps_FIP> oauth-openshift.apps.<cluster name>.<base domain>\n<apps_FIP> prometheus-k8s-openshift-monitoring.apps.<cluster name>.<base domain>\n<apps_FIP> <app name>.apps.<cluster name>.<base domain>"} lang="dns" />
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      </li>
      </ol>
      <h2 id="nw-osp-enabling-ovs-offload_installing-openstack-network-config" class="group scroll-mt-20">Enabling OVS hardware offloading<a href="#nw-osp-enabling-ovs-offload_installing-openstack-network-config" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
